---
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import ClockTester from '../../components/ClockTester.astro';
---

<Tool slug="clock" description="Test MIDI clock and latency in your browser: measure the tempo and jitter of incoming MIDI clock, send clock to a device, and time round trips through a MIDI loopback.">
  <Fragment slot="lede">
    Is your clock steady, and how long does a message take to come back? Measure the tempo and jitter of an
    incoming MIDI clock, drive a device with clock from the browser, and time round trips through a cable or
    virtual loopback.
  </Fragment>
  <ClockTester />
  <Fragment slot="after">
    <Callout title="Reading the numbers">
      <p>
        Times come from Web MIDI event timestamps, so they include the operating system's MIDI stack and the browser,
        not just the cable. At 120 BPM clocks arrive every 20.83 ms; a 5-pin DIN cable needs 0.32 ms to carry one
        clock byte and 0.96 ms for a three-byte message. Jitter under a millisecond is typical for USB MIDI; numbers
        well above that point to a busy computer, a long chain of devices, or a struggling interface. Use the results
        to compare setups on the same machine rather than as absolute truth.
      </p>
    </Callout>
  </Fragment>
</Tool>
